$\underset{\sim}{a}\cdot\underset{\sim}{b} = (6)(1)+(-2)(1) = 4$
$|\underset{\sim}{b}|^{2} = 1+1 = 2$
$\text{proj}_{\underset{\sim}{b}}\underset{\sim}{a} = \dfrac{4}{2}\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}$
$\underset{\sim}{a}-\text{proj}_{\underset{\sim}{b}}\underset{\sim}{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}-\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}$
$= \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix}$
Check: $\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix}\cdot\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = 0$ and $\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$
